WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.930
Previously on Yu-Gi-Oh! VRAINS:

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.320
Soulburner, you will lose this turn.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:08.400
What?

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:11.410
But you won't lose against me.

00:00:11.410 --> 00:00:13.640
You’re going to lose to yourself.

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.610
What do you mean?

00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.340
You're about to find out.

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:22.820
I activate the trap card, 3D Bio Scanner!

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.360
I choose...

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:28.380
Despair from the Dark!

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:47.920
Oh no!  Soulburner’s trauma!

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:50.410
I knew it.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.140
Taking advantage of his 
trauma?  That's not fair!

00:00:54.520 --> 00:00:58.120
I'll do anything to fulfill my goal.

00:00:58.120 --> 00:01:02.130
Especially when my opponent relies on an AI.

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.090
I'll bury you in dark despair.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:12.370
Kusanagi!  How’s the rescue program?

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:13.800
Working on it!

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:20.520
The Ignis program is built 
using a special algorithm.

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:25.970
It's incredible that he decoded 
it and created this trap.

00:01:25.970 --> 00:01:28.980
Giving up, Kusanagi?

00:01:30.080 --> 00:01:32.180
Who do you think I am?

00:01:32.620 --> 00:01:37.170
I'll solve this trap and rescue Soulburner!

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.980
Here's another one!

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:43.980
Here I go!

00:02:00.310 --> 00:02:06.320
Our lives aren't forever

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:13.130
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:02:14.060 --> 00:02:20.410
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:02:20.900 --> 00:02:26.980
Sharing hope for the future

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:33.750
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:40.990
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:47.670
I want to share your pain

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:21.500
Speed Duel!

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.690
I go first!

00:03:24.690 --> 00:03:26.280
My turn!

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:29.020
I summon Gouki Suprex!

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.440
Due to its effect, I Special 
Summon Gouki Riscorpio!

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:41.940
to Special Summon Gouki 
Headbatt in defense position!

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:48.420
Due to Headbatt’s effect, 
Suprex gains 800 ATK!

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:50.880
He also uses a Gouki Deck!

00:03:51.380 --> 00:03:54.580
Appear!  My circuit!

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:58.160
The summoning conditions 
are at least two Goukis!

00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.120
Link Summon!

00:04:00.120 --> 00:04:06.840
Appear, Link 3 Gouki The Solid Ogre!

00:04:06.840 --> 00:04:09.580
Hey, that looks strong.

00:04:09.580 --> 00:04:16.040
Since three Goukis were sent to my graveyard, 
I add three Gouki cards in my deck to my hand.

00:04:16.040 --> 00:04:20.010
I activate the spell card, Gouki Re-Match!

00:04:20.010 --> 00:04:26.730
I Special Summon Gouki Twistcobra and 
Riscorpio from my graveyard in defense position!

00:04:26.730 --> 00:04:30.420
Then I activate the Continuous 
Spell, Gouki Unity!

00:04:31.530 --> 00:04:35.390
When there’s a Gouki Link Monster 
in the Extra Monster Zone...

00:04:35.390 --> 00:04:39.570
...battle nor effects destroy 
Goukis in the Main Monster Zone.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:42.960
And I take 0 damage from Gouki battles.

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:46.850
Hey Playmaker, that’s a solid defense.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.800
I end my turn!

00:04:49.800 --> 00:04:51.040
Battle!

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:56.320
Despair from the Dark attacks 
Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:10.170
The second Despair from the 
Dark attacks you directly!

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:16.300
You're finished!

00:05:16.300 --> 00:05:20.690
The third Despair from the 
Dark attacks you directly!

00:05:22.370 --> 00:05:23.880
Soulburner!

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:27.850
Salamangreat Parro’s effect activates!

00:05:27.850 --> 00:05:32.210
When your monster attacks me 
when I have 1000 or fewer LP...

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:35.560
...it Special Summons itself from my hand!

00:05:38.340 --> 00:05:46.050
When it’s summoned, Parro’s ATK becomes 
the same as a Salamangreat in my graveyard!

00:05:46.050 --> 00:05:49.660
I select Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:06:02.140 --> 00:06:06.400
You survived this strike, 
but you won't next itme.

00:06:07.010 --> 00:06:13.220
The ordeal from the Lost Incident ten 
years ago has left a scar in your heart.

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:21.800
Once your heart is scarred, 
it doesn’t heal easily.

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.170
Especially if it happens during childhood.

00:06:36.520 --> 00:06:40.220
You have no future as a duelist.

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.500
Hand over that Ignis and 
vanish from my sight.

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:50.090
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:50.530 --> 00:06:52.410
Calm down, Soulburner!

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:53.760
Calm down!

00:06:55.840 --> 00:06:59.040
I’ll finish you next turn.

00:06:59.520 --> 00:07:02.370
My turn!  I draw!

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:09.910
I send Stack Reviver in my hand to the 
graveyard to Special Summon Bitrooper!

00:07:09.910 --> 00:07:13.090
Then I summon Cyberse Gadget!

00:07:14.380 --> 00:07:19.650
Due to its effect, I Special Summon Stack 
Reviver from my graveyard in defense position!

00:07:21.320 --> 00:07:24.290
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:07:25.260 --> 00:07:28.010
The summoning conditions are two monsters!

00:07:29.140 --> 00:07:30.370
Link Summon!

00:07:30.720 --> 00:07:34.830
Appear!  Link 2 Security Dragon!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:42.890
Stack Reviver’s effect 
activates from the graveyard!

00:07:42.890 --> 00:07:47.930
Since it was used to Link Summon, I Special 
Summon Cyberse Gadget in defense position!

00:07:47.930 --> 00:07:51.330
Security Dragon’s effect activates!

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.560
I return Gouki Riscorpio to your hand.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:07:58.000
Twistcobra’s effect now activates!

00:07:58.980 --> 00:08:00.760
I tribute Riscorpio!

00:08:01.720 --> 00:08:06.460
Solid Ogre gains ATK 
equal to Riscorpio's ATK!

00:08:08.610 --> 00:08:12.140
Oh no!  4700 is bad, right?

00:08:12.140 --> 00:08:15.140
You made the wrong choice, Playmaker.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:19.880
Instead of Riscorpio, you should 
have returned Solid Ogre.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:24.620
That punk!  He's getting cocky!

00:08:24.620 --> 00:08:31.610
Since Riscorpio was sent to my graveyard, 
its effect adds Suprex from my deck to my hand.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:37.940
Can you overcome these ATK, Playmaker?

00:08:37.940 --> 00:08:41.680
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:46.200
The summoning conditions 
are at least two monsters!

00:08:48.210 --> 00:08:49.740
Link Summon!

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:52.820
Appear, Link 4!

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:58.980
Firewall Dragon!

00:09:01.540 --> 00:09:03.200
Firewall Dragon!

00:09:03.570 --> 00:09:10.700
Since Cyberse Gadget was sent to my 
graveyard, its effect Special Summons a Gadget Token.

00:09:10.700 --> 00:09:14.810
And I Special Summon Backup 
Secretary from my hand!

00:09:16.410 --> 00:09:19.640
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.440
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:24.840
Link Summon!

00:09:24.840 --> 00:09:28.760
Appear, Link 2 Flame Administrator!

00:09:30.520 --> 00:09:35.460
Due to Flame Administrator’s 
effect, Link Monsters gain 800 ATK!

00:09:37.680 --> 00:09:40.160
Firewall Dragon’s effect activates!

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:43.160
Since a monster next to its link 
was sent to the graveyard...

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:47.140
...I Special Summon a monster from my hand!

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:49.500
Come, Dual Assembwurm!

00:09:53.520 --> 00:10:00.180
No matter how many monsters you get, you 
can’t destroy Solid Ogre with its 4700 ATK.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:02.140
Who said I'd destroy it?

00:10:03.380 --> 00:10:07.240
Firewall Dragon’s additional 
effect activates!

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:13.600
For every monster it's co-linked 
with, I return a monster to the hand!

00:10:13.600 --> 00:10:16.320
I return two Goukis!

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.740
Emergency Escape!

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:27.720
The monsters are gone.  Too bad.

00:10:29.130 --> 00:10:30.880
Battle!

00:10:30.880 --> 00:10:35.710
Dual Assembwurm and Firewall 
Dragon attack you directly!

00:10:41.950 --> 00:10:45.060
Tempest Attack!

00:10:53.980 --> 00:10:56.640
Kusanagi, how’s the rescue program?

00:10:58.680 --> 00:11:00.560
Just finished it.

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.910
Now we can free Takeru!

00:11:06.010 --> 00:11:09.110
An error?  No way!

00:11:14.740 --> 00:11:18.320
Someone is trying to break 
Blood Shepherd’s trap.

00:11:20.090 --> 00:11:23.870
It's probably Playmaker's partner.

00:11:23.870 --> 00:11:31.300
Not many people can create a program that 
can destroy Blood Shepherd’s complex trap.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.770
Kusanagi, what happened?

00:11:34.770 --> 00:11:37.510
No good.  It doesn’t activate!

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:41.980
It's mostly done, but his 
finishing touches are lacking.

00:11:43.720 --> 00:11:49.700
If he only knew a bit more about 
Blood Shepherd’s tendencies.

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:54.560
You still want to fight?

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.450
No need to overdo it.

00:11:56.450 --> 00:11:59.640
Just surrender and hand over the Ignis.

00:12:03.260 --> 00:12:04.100
Never!

00:12:04.100 --> 00:12:08.270
You’re acting tough, but 
your soul is in tatters.

00:12:08.270 --> 00:12:10.580
No one'll mock you if you give up.

00:12:10.580 --> 00:12:12.930
My turn!

00:12:12.930 --> 00:12:16.310
When there are no monsters on my field...

00:12:16.310 --> 00:12:23.920
...I target a Fire monster in the graveyard 
and activate the Equip Spell, Rising Fire!

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:29.890
I Special Summon Salamangreat Heatleo 
and equip it with Rising Fire!

00:12:32.890 --> 00:12:37.150
The Field Spell, Salamangreat 
Sanctuary's effect!

00:12:37.860 --> 00:12:41.250
When Link Summoning a 
Salamangreat Link Monster...

00:12:41.250 --> 00:12:47.110
...instead of using Link Materials, I can 
use a monster with the same name on my field!

00:12:48.470 --> 00:12:52.380
Appear!  The circuit that changes the future!

00:12:53.290 --> 00:12:59.720
Surging flame, awaken Heatleo’s true 
strength with the power of purification!

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:03.100
Reincarnation Link Summon!

00:13:05.680 --> 00:13:10.430
Be reborn, the king of beasts that 
runs through the fire prairie!

00:13:10.430 --> 00:13:13.500
Salamangreat Heatleo!

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.660
You're so stubborn.

00:13:17.660 --> 00:13:21.410
No matter what you do now, it’s pointless!

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.890
You’ve already lost.

00:13:24.770 --> 00:13:26.630
Are you sure?

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:34.960
Since the Equip Spell, Rising Fire, left the 
Spell & Trap Zone, its effect activates!

00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:37.960
I select one monster on your field.

00:13:37.960 --> 00:13:43.190
I banish all cards on your field or 
graveyard with the same name as that monster!

00:13:44.200 --> 00:13:46.580
Farewell to despair!

00:13:46.580 --> 00:13:51.520
I select Despair from the Dark!

00:13:53.540 --> 00:13:54.450
What?

00:13:57.650 --> 00:14:04.760
And you take damage equal to the original 
ATK of one of the banished monsters!

00:14:06.990 --> 00:14:09.960
How?  What happened to your trauma?

00:14:09.960 --> 00:14:12.600
Trauma?  What’s he talking about?

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:15.200
I don’t know at all.

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:18.670
What?  Didn't you say...

00:14:19.150 --> 00:14:22.870
Oh no!  Soulburner’s trauma!

00:14:22.870 --> 00:14:25.290
You tricked me!

00:14:25.290 --> 00:14:29.380
You’re the one who said 
it’s foolish to trust an AI.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:32.860
Well?  My acting was pretty good too, right?

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:36.090
Ignoring me?

00:14:44.190 --> 00:14:46.430
You got one over him.

00:14:46.430 --> 00:14:54.410
You stomped all over my heart and looked 
into the memories hidden in my soul!

00:14:54.410 --> 00:15:00.140
But he hid the most important 
thing using self control.

00:15:05.580 --> 00:15:08.060
You did that on purpose.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:10.450
Thank you, Flame.

00:15:13.990 --> 00:15:15.850
Calm down, Takeru Homura!

00:15:15.850 --> 00:15:19.510
What’s with him?  He's suddenly scared.

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:22.200
Did he just realize how strong I am?

00:15:22.200 --> 00:15:24.390
Well, it doesn’t matter.

00:15:24.390 --> 00:15:26.950
I’ll continue the duel.

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:30.370
I summon Skull Conductor from my hand!

00:15:33.280 --> 00:15:38.420
Battle!  Skull Conductor 
attacks Valkyrian Knight!

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.750
The Field Spell, Edge of Darkness activates!

00:15:42.750 --> 00:15:51.170
When a Zombie attacks, it gains 100 
ATK for every Zombie on the field!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:04.750
Takeru Homura!  Are you okay?

00:16:04.750 --> 00:16:11.180
Then Despair from the Dark 
attacks Phoenix Gearfried!

00:16:11.180 --> 00:16:16.560
Due to the Field Spell, Edge of 
Darkness’s effect, it gains 200 ATK!

00:16:19.690 --> 00:16:23.140
Please stop!  I can’t take it anymore!

00:16:23.140 --> 00:16:25.500
You’re giving up?

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.100
Don't quit!

00:16:27.100 --> 00:16:28.730
You can still fight!

00:16:28.730 --> 00:16:32.130
You’re not as weak as you think.

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:36.280
I can’t do anything when 
that monster appears.

00:16:36.280 --> 00:16:38.720
That’s just in your head!

00:16:39.790 --> 00:16:43.380
You believe it’s your fault 
that your parents died.

00:16:43.380 --> 00:16:46.710
And you linked that with the 
fear of being forced to duel.

00:16:46.710 --> 00:16:49.850
And you closed off your heart!

00:16:49.850 --> 00:16:54.590
After the battle ends, Skull 
Conductor's own effect destroys it.

00:16:57.060 --> 00:17:01.540
I set one card and end my turn.

00:17:01.540 --> 00:17:06.380
Don't be scared!  Face yourself!

00:17:08.280 --> 00:17:10.680
Your life is only beginning!

00:17:10.680 --> 00:17:13.570
Be reborn and seize your future!

00:17:14.510 --> 00:17:16.650
Stand up, Takeru Homura!

00:17:16.650 --> 00:17:18.310
Be courageous!

00:17:18.310 --> 00:17:20.250
Reincarnate, Takeru!

00:17:28.480 --> 00:17:31.500
My turn!  I draw!

00:17:31.990 --> 00:17:35.840
I activate the Equip Spell, Rising Fire!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:42.980
I Special Summon Phoenix Gearfried 
and equip it with this card!

00:17:46.680 --> 00:17:50.760
And I activate the spell card, Tempest Fire!

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:59.480
I destroy all monsters on my field, and we 
both take damage equal to its original ATK!

00:17:59.480 --> 00:18:00.360
What?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:07.620
And your monster with equal or lower 
ATK than Gearfried is destroyed!

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.450
And you take damage equal to half its ATK!

00:18:11.450 --> 00:18:12.700
What?

00:18:12.700 --> 00:18:15.710
I’ve decided to be reborn.

00:18:16.180 --> 00:18:20.440
I destroy Despair from the Dark!

00:18:21.760 --> 00:18:24.220
No way!

00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:29.220
I did it!  I won!

00:18:29.220 --> 00:18:31.200
Well done, Takeru!

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:35.160
Your indomitable soul 
hasn’t burned out yet.

00:18:35.160 --> 00:18:37.650
It’s all thanks to you-

00:18:37.650 --> 00:18:39.410
Do you have a name?

00:18:39.410 --> 00:18:42.400
How rude!  Of course I do!

00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:45.540
My name is Flame, the fire Ignis.

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.120
Written as "indomitable soul 
dream," pronounced Flame.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:52.120
"Flame" is "fire" in English, right?

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:54.490
You just forced it into kanji.

00:18:57.450 --> 00:18:58.830
Ignoring me?

00:18:58.830 --> 00:19:02.220
I overcame my trauma long ago!

00:19:02.940 --> 00:19:05.630
What you saw was my past!

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:09.130
I’m far beyond that!

00:19:10.490 --> 00:19:15.140
You thought you found my weakness by 
looking at my memories, but you didn't.

00:19:15.140 --> 00:19:23.070
When Heatleo is Link Summoned, one card in 
your Spell & Trap Zone returns to your deck!

00:19:23.070 --> 00:19:26.480
I return Drone Barricade!

00:19:26.480 --> 00:19:28.580
But I banish that card!

00:19:28.580 --> 00:19:33.780
And I can set a new Drone Barricade 
from my deck and activate it this turn!

00:19:33.780 --> 00:19:37.250
Salamangreat Foxer’s effect activates!

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.260
When there’s a card in 
your Spell & Trap Zone...

00:19:40.260 --> 00:19:44.750
...and there are at least three 
Salamangreats in my graveyard...

00:19:44.750 --> 00:19:46.930
...it sends itself to the graveyard

00:19:46.930 --> 00:19:50.700
to return a Salamangreat in my 
graveyard to the Extra Deck!

00:19:50.700 --> 00:19:55.940
And I select a card in your Spell 
& Trap Zone and destroy it!

00:19:55.940 --> 00:19:59.610
I select Drone Barricade!

00:20:00.410 --> 00:20:06.350
You can now attack him directly, 
but he still has a set card.

00:20:09.000 --> 00:20:11.560
What's wrong?  Scared?

00:20:13.370 --> 00:20:16.510
I made a decision!

00:20:17.560 --> 00:20:21.120
To take a new step forward with Flame!

00:20:21.120 --> 00:20:24.000
With an AI?  Don’t make me laugh.

00:20:24.780 --> 00:20:28.870
A duelist like you must vanish from my sight.

00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.350
Go ahead and try.

00:20:31.350 --> 00:20:32.580
Battle!

00:20:32.580 --> 00:20:36.280
Salamangreat Heatleo attacks you directly!

00:20:42.500 --> 00:20:45.720
What?  The program is rewritten?

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:02.580
What’s happening?

00:21:02.580 --> 00:21:04.690
The area is disappearing.

00:21:05.010 --> 00:21:06.290
Damn!

00:21:09.140 --> 00:21:12.160
Wait!  The duel isn’t over yet!

00:21:12.160 --> 00:21:13.710
Running away?

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:23.870
Soulburner!

00:21:28.760 --> 00:21:32.270
C'mon!  Just when I was about to win.

00:21:32.270 --> 00:21:34.020
I’m glad you’re okay.

00:21:34.600 --> 00:21:37.620
Kusanagi, I reunited with Soulburner.

00:21:37.620 --> 00:21:39.150
We'll log out.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:40.020
Okay.

00:21:45.500 --> 00:21:47.940
I told you not to interfere.

00:21:47.940 --> 00:21:50.740
But who was about to lose?

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:53.480
If you didn’t interfere, I would've won.

00:21:53.480 --> 00:21:56.160
If you say so.

00:21:56.980 --> 00:22:01.590
If you’re going to interfere, 
you’re my enemy, Ghost Girl!

00:22:19.900 --> 00:22:26.240
Memories that don't disappear
And memories that disappeared

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:32.940
I quietly "NOW LOADING..." those scenes

00:22:33.370 --> 00:22:36.440
Memories left behind  Erased memories

